# ~/.config/logincookies/rules: which cookies are login cookies, ahead of
# logincookies' own guess from the cookie names. One rule a line:
#
#   NAME     a cookie named NAME is a login cookie, on any site
#            (* matches any characters, upper and lower case are the same)
#   !NAME    a cookie named NAME never is
#   @SITE    every cookie of SITE and of its subdomains is one
#   !@SITE   no cookie of SITE is one
#
# The rules saying no come first. `logincookies list -a` while the browser
# runs lists its cookies and marks the login cookies with *: log in, look
# for the site's cookies there, and add the ones that are missing.
# The rules are read when logincookies starts.

# A site whose login cookies have names of their own: keep all its cookies.
#@daum.net

# One more cookie name.
#my_login_cookie

# A cookie that only looks like a login cookie.
#!lang_session
